maria: Heads-up — I opened a PR to standardize the v1->v2 examples across languages. The JS/py snippets diverged and are confusing customers. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/842 :eyes:
chris: thanks — saw the diff. main issue is the old `models.invoke` vs new `client.responses.create` patterns in examples. also curl has an outdated header name.
sarah: can we avoid a full rewrite? maybe add a short compatibility note and side-by-side examples instead of replacing everything at once. some customers rely on the v1 shim. :thinking_face: maria: we should prefer canonical v2 examples but keep a tiny compatibility block. proposal in PR: top of each page has a single-line note and a collapsible "v1 -> v2 mapping". chris: sounds good. also we need devkit snippets: go, ruby — currently only js/py. can we add minimal snippets for those languages? ben: I can add Go and Ruby quick snippets. will follow the same request/response shape. estimate ~2 hours. jennifer: FYI, docs-ci-bot failed on one example: the streaming snippet used obsolete framing code. docs-ci-bot: [ci] example-lint failed on file examples/streaming.md: missing streamChunk handler. maria: thanks @docs-ci-bot — Ben, can you also fix streaming while you add Go/Ruby? ben: yep will fix streaming handler and update tests. sarah: for the side-by-side mapping, can we include a short table mapping common params: model_id -> model, output_format -> type, etc. simple bullet list is fine. chris: also check model alias changes — old embed model `embed-legacy-512` is now `rwd-embed-512-v2`. add a migration note in embeddings.md. maria: agreed. action items: (1) Ben: add Go/Ruby + streaming fix + update CI examples; (2) Chris: update embeddings.md alias note and add one-liner in the embed quickstart; (3) Sarah: write the v1->v2 mapping collapsible snippet and add to top of guide pages; (4) Maria: review and merge PR once green. jen: tagging docs reviewers: @chris @sarah — please review Ben's follow-up when he pushes. docs-ci-bot: [ci] PR 842 — updated example tests queued. ETA ~15m. maria: small example change we want in the JS snippet (old):
```js
// v1 style
const res = await client.models.invoke({ model: 'gpt-3.5', input: 'hi' })
```
replace with v2 canonical:
```js
// v2 canonical
const res = await client.responses.create({ model: 'gpt-4o-mini', input: 'hi' })
```
chris: good. please also show how to stream responses in v2 (two-line snippet). maria: added short streaming example in the PR:
```js
const stream = await client.responses.stream({ model: 'gpt-4o-mini', input: 'long prompt' })
for await (const chunk of stream) { process.stdout.write(chunk.delta) }
``` sarah: remember to call out that function-tool-calling signature changed slightly. add a note about `tools` vs `functions`. ben: pushed Go and Ruby snippets + streaming fix. PR updated. link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/842/files chris: running the local smoke tests now. embedding alias note pushed to embeddings.md — include reference to the alias map JSON. maria: awesome. if CI passes, let's merge by EOD. small comms note: product wants a short line in deprecation email announcing docs alignment. Sarah can draft. sarah: will draft email and a short doc changelog blurb. maria: thanks all — will merge after approvals. :shipit:
